Title:
ETWInspector

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
ETWInspector is a C#-based PowerShell module for enumerating and inspecting Event Tracing for Windows (ETW) providers and trace sessions, and for capturing ETW traces. It supports discovery of Manifest, MOF, and TraceLogging providers, including scanning binaries for embedded TraceLogging metadata via the `ETW0` signature. The toolkit adds snapshotting and diffing (`Export-EtwSnapshot`, `Compare-EtwSnapshot`) to track how provider definitions/events change across Windows builds, machines, or updates, with deterministic JSON/NDJSON output optimized for clean diffs. It also exposes provider security descriptors and can query trace sessions locally/remotely. The project documents important TraceLogging limitations (no reliable per-event provider binding from metadata alone) and points to static-analysis approaches when attribution is required. Useful for red teams, malware researchers, and defenders who need to understand ETW telemetry surface area, validate detections, or monitor OS/provider drift over time.

Technical Focus:
- ETW provider enumeration (Manifest, MOF, TraceLogging)
- TraceLogging metadata discovery via `ETW0` scanning in PE binaries
- Snapshot/export of provider schemas and event metadata (JSON/NDJSON)
- Structured diffing of ETW provider/event changes across systems/versions
- ETW trace session inspection and capture control
- ETW provider security descriptors / access control

Use Cases:
- Baseline ETW providers/events on a host and diff after Windows updates to identify new/changed telemetry
- Identify high-value providers/keywords/events (e.g., Threat Intelligence) for detection engineering or evasion research
- Inventory TraceLogging providers embedded in specific DLL/EXE/SYS files (including custom app directories)
- Validate whether an endpoint has expected ETW providers enabled/available and how they’re secured
- Start/stop targeted ETW captures during tool execution to study emitted events

Keywords:
ETW, Event Tracing for Windows, PowerShell module, C#, Manifest providers, MOF providers, TraceLogging, ETW0 signature, Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent, provider enumeration, trace sessions, Start-EtwCapture, Stop-EtwCapture, Get-EtwProviders, Get-EtwTraceSessions, security descriptor, Export-EtwSnapshot, Compare-EtwSnapshot, NDJSON, Windows telemetry